{
  "code": "HUMBI-BS",
  "reviewed": "2026-10-23",
  "summary": "The audit checks the 81 units: the six HumBio core courses (HUMBIO 2A, 2B, 3A, 3B, 4A and 4B, letter graded), one statistics course (letter graded), three upper-division HumBio or listed Overseas Studies courses of 3 or more units (one of them may be CR/NC, the others letter graded), the WIM (the B-side core courses) and one capstone option. Every letter-graded course needs a C- or better, and honors needs HUMBIO 193 and a B+ or better in HUMBIO 194. Checked by hand: the 20 units of breadth and five depth courses approved by the HumBio advising team (depth letter graded, 3 or more units each, three departments), the BS-designated courses, Interdisciplinary Honors, the non-PWR Notation elective, and transfer credit, which has its own limits per requirement.",
